 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "coordinates lists the route waypoints [x, y] (integers); consecutive waypoints are distinct and every segment has an integer length (this keeps positions exact). For each d in distances, the position is the point reached after travelling d along the polyline from the first waypoint; when d is at least the route length the position is the last waypoint. Return, for each d, the index of the waypoint nearest to that position by Euclidean distance (any waypoint of the route, not only the segment ends), the smallest index on a tie.",
